# Public algorithms, Metal mapping

Every equation in a pipeline comes from a public paper, spec, or vendor document, then mapped onto a Metal op this machine actually runs. Another repository's source, tests, comments, or design notes are not a reference. Porting them pulls in that runtime's layout and hides the Metal mapping.

Score a formula on this runtime's own forward. An int4 argmax is not evidence the equation is right. Check the BF16 shader dot of the checkpoint values.

Record the citation in REFERENCES.md and the as-built form in ARCHITECTURE.md.

## Examples

Wrong: open another runtime's n-gram forward and copy its hash so the tokens match.

Right: Cheng et al. eq. (6) for the branch gate, the tech report's `1/n_r` on the residual read, and a Metal float dot of the stored matrix.
